            [
                'title' => 'The Importance of Mobile-First Design',
                'slug' => 'importance-mobile-first-design',
                'content' => '<h2>Why Mobile-First Matters</h2><p>With mobile devices accounting for over 50% of web traffic, adopting a mobile-first approach is no longer optional—it is essential.</p><h2>Benefits of Mobile-First Design</h2><p><strong>1. Better User Experience:</strong> Mobile-first design ensures that your website works perfectly on the devices people actually use.</p><p><strong>2. Improved SEO:</strong> Search engines prioritize mobile-friendly websites in their rankings.</p><p><strong>3. Faster Load Times:</strong> Starting with mobile constraints leads to leaner, faster websites.</p><p><strong>4. Future-Proofing:</strong> A mobile foundation scales up better than desktop designs scaled down.</p><h2>Implementation Tips</h2><ul><li>Start with the smallest screen size</li><li>Use responsive design principles</li><li>Optimize images and assets</li><li>Prioritize core functionality</li><li>Test on real devices</li></ul><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Mobile-first design is not just a trend—it is a fundamental approach to creating successful digital products.</p>',
                'meta_title' => 'The Importance of Mobile-First Design',
