            [
                'title' => 'Choosing the Right Technology Stack',
                'slug' => 'choosing-technology-stack',
                'content' => '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>Selecting the right technology stack is one of the most important decisions in web development. It can make or break your project success.</p><h2>Factors to Consider</h2><h3>1. Project Requirements</h3><p>Consider the scope, complexity, and specific needs of your project. What features do you need? What are your performance requirements?</p><h3>2. Team Expertise</h3><p>What technologies does your team already know? Training takes time and resources.</p><h3>3. Community and Support</h3><p>Popular technologies have larger communities, more resources, and better long-term support.</p><h3>4. Scalability</h3><p>Will the technology scale as your application grows? Consider both horizontal and vertical scaling.</p><h3>5. Security</h3><p>Security should never be an afterthought. Choose technologies with strong security records.</p><h2>Popular Stack Options</h2><p><strong>LAMP Stack:</strong> Time-tested, widely supported, and cost-effective.</p><p><strong>MEAN/MERN Stack:</strong> JavaScript-based, great for real-time applications.</p><p><strong>Laravel Stack:</strong> PHP-based with excellent developer experience and ecosystem.</p><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> The "best" stack depends on your specific needs. Take the time to evaluate all factors before making your decision.</p>',
                'meta_title' => 'Choosing the Right Technology Stack',
                'meta_description' => 'A comprehensive guide to selecting the best technology stack for your project.',
                'published' => true,
                'user_id' => $admin->id,
